Boxer
-----

The node runs Boxer by Meta (https://github.com/facebookresearch/boxer): BoxerNet, its DINOv3 and OWLv2 parts, and
the checkpoints. Boxer's code and checkpoints are under CC BY-NC 4.0. Boxer's own LICENSE and NOTICE (with the
licences of the parts Boxer contains) are in third_party/boxer, a git submodule at a fixed commit. tools/setup.sh
downloads the checkpoints from Hugging Face (facebook/boxer). This repository contains no copy of Boxer's code or
checkpoints.

Adapted from Boxer
------------------

sdp_from_depth in src/xblick_boxer/boxer.py is adapted from BaseLoader.sdp_from_depth in Boxer's
loaders/base_loader.py. Both compute the semi-dense points of a depth image in the world: the same grid step, the same
pinhole unprojection, the same rotation and translation into the world, at most num_samples points, padded with NaN
to num_samples. The changes:

- It takes the depth image as a PyTorch tensor and computes with PyTorch on the tensor's device (the GPU in the
  node). Boxer's function takes a NumPy array and computes with NumPy on the CPU.
- It takes the grid's pixels by strided slicing and torch.meshgrid. Boxer's function uses numpy.mgrid and index
  arrays. Both take the same pixels.
- It chooses the points above num_samples with torch.randperm on the device. Boxer's function uses
  numpy.random.choice without replacement. Both choose uniformly without replacement, with different random numbers.
- It returns the points on the device of the depth image. Boxer's function returns a CPU tensor.
- It has no case for a missing depth image. Boxer's function returns an empty tensor for None. The node calls it only
  with a depth image.
